{"permDenialCache causes Check() to return deny immediately before consulting the DB or permCache, and relies solely on TTL-based eviction with no explicit invalidation, causing stale denial entries to persist and incorrectly block legitimate requests until TTL expires": 0.8935174345970154, "cacheWrap exposes no Delete method, so denial entries written by Check() cannot be explicitly cleared when permissions change, causing Check() to short-circuit to deny until TTL expiry when backing store is updated to grant access": 0.8704531192779541, "ProvideAuthZClient constructs the in-proc authzlib client with a NoopCache while newRemoteRBACClient uses a real 30-second local cache, creating behavioral and performance divergence between in-proc and remote deployments": 0.7957285046577454, "NoopCache is passed to authzlib.WithCacheClientOption but the external authlib cache.Cache interface definition is not visible in this repository; if the interface requires additional methods or different signatures, the program will fail to compile or panic at runtime": 0.07424280047416687, "The removed cache-hit test in TestService_getUserPermissions is not replaced, leaving no assertions that getUserPermissions populates permCache or that singleflight deduplication works": 0.34566980600357056, "New TestService_CacheCheck/CacheList tests omit TTL/eviction and concurrent-access scenarios": 0.13000066578388214}